ng jump distances, in centimeters, that the girls team of Pseudo H.S. made at practice today. $(51|1$ represents $511$ centimeters$.)$ What is the sum of the median and mode of the data?\n\n\\begin{tabular}{l|lllll}\n51& 1\\\\\n52&\\\\\n53& 2& 5\\\\\n54& 0& 2& 2& 5\\\\\n55& 0& 1& 3& 4& 7\\\\\n56& 0& 2& 5\\\\\n57& 0& 1\\\\\n\\end{tabular}","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"a70eb1cd78ec5d8fcf5a0819e4f39ea7df5428123323e1a8d346acb2f15d6ef9"},"seconds":17.61717915534973,"seed":599653202431435071,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we first need to interpret and organize the data from the stem and leaf plot. Each row in the plot represents a stem (the tens digit) and the leaves (the ones digit) represent the individual measurements.\n\nThe stem and leaf plot provided can be expanded as follows:\n- 511 cm (from 51|1)\n- 520 cm (from 52|)\n- 532 cm (from 53|2)\n- 535 cm (from 53|5)\n- 540 cm (from 54|0)\n- 542 cm (from 54|2)\n- 542 cm (from 54|2)\n- 545 cm (from 54|5)\n- 550 cm (from 55|0)\n- 551 cm (from 55|1)\n- 553 cm (from 55|3)\n- 554 cm (from 55|4)\n- 557 cm (from 55|7)\n- 560 cm (from 56|0)\n- 562 cm (from 56|2)\n- 565 cm (from 56|5)\n- 570 cm (from 57|0)\n- 571 cm (from 57|1)\n\nThus, the complete list of long jump distances is:\n\\[ 511, 520, 532, 535, 540, 542, 542, 545, 550, 551, 553, 554, 557, 560, 562, 565, 570, 571 \\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the median and mode of this data set.\n\n### Step 1: Finding the Median\nThe median is the middle value of an ordered list. Since there are 18 data points (an even number), the median is the average of the 9th and 10th values in the ordered list.\n\nThe 9th value is 550 cm, and the 10th value is 551 cm. Therefore, the median is:\n\\[ \\text{Median} = \\frac{550 + 551}{2} = \\frac{1101}{2} = 550.5 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Finding the Mode\nThe mode is the value that appears most frequently in the data set. From the list, we can see that the number 542 appears twice, and no other number appears more frequently. Therefore, the mode is:\n\\[ \\text{Mode} = 542 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Sum of the Median and Mode\nFinally, we sum the median and the mode:\n\\[ \\text{Sum} = 550.5 + 542 = 1092.5 \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the median and mode of the data is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1092.5} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1092.5}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:93"}
